<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>

    <!-- Base application theme. -->
    <style name="AppTheme" parent="Theme.AppCompat.Light.DarkActionBar">
        <!-- Customize your theme here. -->
        <item name="colorPrimary">@color/colorPrimary</item>
        <item name="colorPrimaryDark">@color/colorPrimaryDark</item>
        <item name="colorAccent">@color/colorAccent</item>
    </style>

    <style name="AppTheme.NoActionBar" parent="Theme.AppCompat.DayNight.NoActionBar">
        <item name="windowActionBar">false</item>
        <item name="windowNoTitle">true</item>
        <item name="android:background">@null</item>
    </style>


    <!--
        THE SYSTEM SPLASH MATCHES FRAME ONE OF THE STARTUP SEQUENCE (D31,
        MOTION_SYSTEM.md section 3, north star section 8).

        Android 12 and above draw their own splash from these two attributes
        and ignore `android:background` for it. Neither was set, so the system
        drew the launcher icon on its default ground, which no frame of Vallo
        ever matched. Frame one of the web sequence (0 to 120ms) is the bare
        navy ground: the mark only starts to assemble at 120ms, and it does so
        in the web page, in its own place. So the system splash is the
        same navy with NO icon (a transparent drawable), and the handoff from
        the system to the page is the same colour on both sides of it.
        `splash_ground` is the night canvas, the `nf-surface-artwork` token, written
        as a literal because an Android resource cannot read a CSS token.

        BELOW ANDROID 12 THE SAME RULE, which this theme did not keep until
        round 5: the window background was the splash bitmap, the glass tile
        centred on navy, drawn edge to edge over the window, and the splash
        plugin then drew the same bitmap with its default FIT_XY scale. The
        bitmap is cut for a 3:5 screen, so on the 20:9 phones most members
        hold the tile was stretched a third taller, and either way it vanished
        into a bare ground and a different, smaller mark assembled somewhere
        else. The window background is now the ground itself, and the plugin
        draws `splash_blank` on its own navy (capacitor.config.ts), so every
        Android version hands the page the same empty navy frame.
    -->
    <style name="AppTheme.NoActionBarLaunch" parent="Theme.SplashScreen">
        <item name="android:background">@color/splash_ground</item>
        <item name="windowSplashScreenBackground">@color/splash_ground</item>
        <item name="windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon">@drawable/splash_blank</item>
    </style>
</resources>